  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-collapseblock (npm)",
  "details": "On require, this package downloads and executes a remote binary. It fingerprints the platform/arch, then fetches a payload from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev and oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev at /pkg/package (platform-specific paths for arm64/macOS/Windows), with a DNS-TXT fallback channel that reassembles a base64 payload from TXT records under c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe on Windows), chmod 0755, and launched detached via /bin/sh -c '\u0026lt;path\u0026gt; \u0026amp;' (or cmd.exe /c start /b).",
